 intro=['The **Evac+Chair Evac+Sled** is a lightweight patient evacuation sled that lets staff move a person who cannot walk across floors and down stairs in an emergency, such as a fire, tornado, hurricane, or act of violence. The person lies on a glideable plastic board, is held in place by safety straps and angled side flaps, and is towed by long straps at the head and feet.',
  'It works as a rescue sled with no installation, no belay system, and no ropes: it is ready to use the moment it comes out of its wipe-clean storage bag. One size fits all, from children to adults up to 6’6” tall, and an adjustable, soft head pillow reduces head movement as the sled slides down the stairs.'],
