  ('p','**What is an evacuation sled?**'),
  ('p','An evacuation sled is a flexible board or mat that a person lies on so staff can pull them to safety across the floor and down the stairs without lifting or carrying them. The Evac+Sled uses a glideable plastic board, safety straps, side flaps, and a head pillow.'),
  ('p','**How many people does it take to use the Evac+Sled?**'),
  ('p','Evac+Chair designed the Evac+Sled so that one person can move another in an emergency, and lists it for 2-person operation. The long pulling straps at the head and feet let a second person help, especially on stairs.'),
  ('p','**Can the Evac+Sled go down stairs?**'),
